A spec that sets `ui: true` needs a sketch of the interface before the interface is
built:

    ilk html-wireframe new "Checkout — payment step"

Draw it in `{{ index .Caps "wireframe.sketches" }}/` and link it from a `## Wireframe`
section, one per screen or state the spec introduces. Layout and flow only — no colour,
no final copy, no behaviour. A sketch that looks finished gets reactions about the shade
of a button; one that looks like a sketch gets reactions about the flow.

Each wireframe is one HTML file that opens from disk with no network and no build, so
whoever inherits this can still see what was agreed.

Say what you want disagreed with. A wireframe with no question attached gets "looks
good" and settles nothing.
